│     "abstract": "OBJECTIVE To assess the value and impact of a screening programme for Down's syndrome that uses the │
│ two maternal serum markers: alpha fetoprotein and free beta human chorionic gonadotrophin. DESIGN All women booked   │
│ into clinics were screened. Further tests were offered to women with a risk of one in 300 or greater of having an    │
│ affected baby. Follow up of outcome of all pregnancies. SETTING Biochemical screening laboratory serving two health  │
│ districts. SUBJECTS 8179 women of all ages with singleton pregnancies screened between 15 and 22 weeks' gestation    │
│ from 1 April 1991 to 31 March 1992. MAIN OUTCOME MEASURES Detection rate of Down's syndrome, false positive rate,    │
