│ (95% confidence interval 6.4 to 60.5), p < 0.00001. In a pregnancy with a 1 in 270 triple-screen risk for Down       │
│ syndrome, normal biometric and anatomic results reduce the risk to 1 in 2100. CONCLUSION Normal ultrasonographic     │
