subjects who had negative screening results for test center, maternal age, and specimen date. The risks for adverse     
perinatal outcomes were compared. RESULTS Women with double-positive screening results had significantly higher risks of
having fetuses with structural abnormalities (odds ratio, 14.5) and chromosomal anomalies (odds ratio, 36.3). They also 
