### 3. Additional context (if relevant):
The selection criteria required studies evaluating maternal urine tests for Down's syndrome up to 24 weeks gestation 
compared with a reference standard. Five studies met all criteria:
- Study 202: Urinary free beta-hCG and beta-core hCG (13 DS cases)
- Study 204: Urinary hyperglycosylated hCG/H-hCG in first trimester (8 DS cases)
- Study 277: Urinary gonadotropin peptide/UGP in second trimester (14 DS cases)
- Study 297: Urinary beta-core fragment fresh samples (23 DS cases)
- Study 300: Urinary gonadotropin peptide in Asian women (29 DS cases)

Study 241 was excluded as it established reference ranges in healthy pregnancies without evaluating Down syndrome cases.
Study 296 was excluded as it focused on nuchal translucency ultrasound, not urine testing. The majority of studies 
utilized maternal serum markers or ultrasound measurements and were therefore excluded.

