│ normal fetuses.   Conclusions The integrated test detects more cases of Down\'s syndrome with a much lower false     │
│ positive rate than the best currently available test.  The New England Journal Of Medicine"}, {"study_index": 396,   │
│ "title": "A six year study of the antenatal detection of fetal abnormality in six Scottish health boards",           │
│ "abstract": "OBJECTIVE To assess the sensitivity of prenatal diagnosis by ultrasound and biochemical methods, to     │
│ evaluate the reasons for non-detection and to make appropriate recommendations. DESIGN Six year observational study, │
│ during which biochemical screening for trisomy 21 was introduced and there was an increase in routine ultrasound     │
