gonadotropin (hCG) multiple of the median (MOM) of 480 Down syndrome cases in the second trimester was 2.64,            
significantly greater than the reported median MOM of intact hCG (p < 0.0001). In 234 of these cases from retrospective 
and prospective studies, the effectiveness of maternal serum free beta hCG was evaluated in combination with            
alpha-fetoprotein (AFP) and maternal age in second-trimester Down syndrome screening. Down syndrome detection in the    
gestational age range of 14-16 weeks was 82 per cent. In all gestational weeks (14-22), a 77.7 per cent Down syndrome   
detection rate was achieved. In prospective screening of 44,272 patients under the age of 35 years, 69 per cent of Down 
syndrome cases were detected (73 per cent in gestational weeks 14-16). The false-positive rate for the prospective study
