in the prospective arm of the study. There was no reduction of overall screening performance compared with our current  
first‐trimester combined screening program. The number of intermediate‐risk pregnancies was sufficiently low as to      
enable advanced ultrasound scanning by well‐trained sonographers only.   Conclusion In population screening for fetal   
trisomy 21, sequential triage in the first trimester can be achieved using very simple methods. Pregnancies at high or  
