│ 442, 443], "studies": [{"study_index": 401, "title": "Maternal serum free alpha‐human chorionic gonadotrophin levels │
│ in twin pregnancies: implications for screening for Down's syndrome", "abstract": "Maternal serum free alpha-human   │
│ chorionic gonadotrophin (free alpha-hCG) levels were determined in twin and singleton pregnancies at 15-22 weeks of  │
│ gestation using a set of stored serum samples relating to 200 twin pregnancies and 600 singleton control pregnancies │
